function auditWriteEpLlrFormulaAudit(path,~)
%AUDITWRITEEPLLRFORMULAAUDIT Static implementation trace, not a model change.
f=fopen(path,'w','n','UTF-8');assert(f>=0);cleanup=onCleanup(@()fclose(f));
fprintf(f,['EP-to-LLR implementation audit\n\nDimensions: y in C^(Nr x 1), Hhat in C^(Nr x Nt), Nt=Nr=2, constellation A has 16 unit-average-power QAM points. ' ...
'For every valid data RE, bitLlr is [Nt x 4], then transposed into llrGrid [4 bit x 2 stream x 48 data-subcarrier x 507 OFDM-symbol].\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['1. Posterior Gaussian at EP iteration t (auditEpDetectorOjcd, equations (10)-(14))\n' ...
'Lambda_t = Hhat^H Hhat / noiseVar + diag(lambda_t), Sigma_t = Lambda_t^{-1}, mu_t = Sigma_t (Hhat^H y / noiseVar + gamma_t). ' ...
'posterior Gaussian variance before the discrete projection is diag(Sigma_t), size Nt x 1. noiseVar is the only explicit observation-noise variance term.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['2. Cavity/extrinsic moments\n' ...
'v_e = sigmaDiag ./ (1 - sigmaDiag .* lambda), x_e = v_e .* (mu ./ sigmaDiag - gamma), both Nt x 1. ' ...
'If a denominator is too small it is replaced by precisionFloor; nonfinite or too-small v_e is replaced by 1/precisionFloor.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['3. Discrete 16QAM posterior\n' ...
'q_i(a) proportional to exp(-|x_e,i-a|^2 / max(real(v_e,i),varianceFloor)); log weights are shifted by max_a before exp, so this is stable exact normalization, not max-log. ' ...
'x_p,i = sum_a q_i(a)a; v_p,i = max(real(sum_a q_i(a)|a|^2-|x_p,i|^2),varianceFloor). posteriorSymbolVariance stored by the receiver is v_p, size [2 streams x 48 x 507].\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['4. EP site update and extrinsic wording\n' ...
'lambdaCandidate = 1/v_p - 1/v_e; gammaCandidate = x_p/v_p - x_e/v_e; negative/nonfinite candidates roll back to prior lambda/gamma, then lambda and gamma are damped with beta=0.2. ' ...
'There is no decoder prior LLR input and no LDPC-to-EP feedback in this frozen path; lambda/gamma are EP site parameters, not reused decoder priors.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['5. Bit LLRs\n' ...
'For QAM bit b, P0=sum_{a in A_b0}q_i(a), P1=sum_{a in A_b1}q_i(a), L_i,b=log(max(P0,realmin))-log(max(P1,realmin)). ' ...
'Positive L means bit 0. This is exact log-sum over the normalized discrete posterior, not a max-log approximation.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['6. Variance sources and omissions\n' ...
'AWGN enters only through noiseVar in Hhat^H Hhat/noiseVar and Hhat^H y/noiseVar. No explicit residual-interference variance term is added. ' ...
'No channel-estimation uncertainty covariance is added to Lambda, v_e, v_p, or the bit metric. varianceFloor=1e-12 and precisionFloor=1e-12 are active in code. Negative/nonfinite site precision is not silent: it is counted and rolled back; raw chunks do not retain those counters or v_e/v_p per RE.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['7. Method comparison\n' ...
'PerfectCSI, BaseKalman, FixedRadius3 and CovarianceAware all call auditMechanismOnlineReceive -> auditEpDetectorOjcd with the same noiseVar, constellation, EP options, variance floors and LLR formula. ' ...
'They differ through Hhat only. OJCD calls auditOjcdTwoLayerSymbol and runs the same auditEpDetectorOjcd twice; finalExtrinsicLlr is the second EP output, again with the same noiseVar and formula. ' ...
'Thus OJCD differs through its two-stage Hdata construction and the fact that the final second-pass EP is used, not through an explicit alternate LLR variance definition.\n']);
end
